$BD$ is a diameter, so $ABCD$ has right angles at $A$ and $C$. $AB = 9$ cm, $AD = 12$ cm and $BC = 12$ cm. Find $DC$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.798,0.877);
\coordinate (B) at (-0.347,1.97);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.798,-0.877);
\coordinate (D) at (0.347,-1.97);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (B) -- (D);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\node[right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[left] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at ($(A)!0.5!(B)$) {$9\text{ cm}$};
\node[below right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at ($(A)!0.5!(D)$) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\node[above left, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at ($(B)!0.5!(C)$) {$12\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral with centre $O$, and side $CD$ is extended to $E$. $\angle AOC = 160^{\circ}$. Find the exterior angle $\angle ADE$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-1.532,1.286);
\coordinate (B) at (1.532,1.286);
\coordinate (C) at (1,-1.732);
\coordinate (D) at (-1.414,-1.414);
\coordinate (E) at (-2.863,-1.223);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\draw (D) -- (E);
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (C);
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below] at (E) {$E$};
\pic[draw, "x", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = A--D--E};
\pic[draw, "160^{\circ}", angle radius=0.55cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = C--O--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

